              "text": "ਚੌਲ (chaul) is a tadbhava, a word inherited and reshaped by sound change. It comes from cāvala, \"husked rice\", a form CDIAL reconstructs from its descendants (CDIAL 4749). CDIAL thinks it possibly shares a non-Aryan origin with Sanskrit taṇḍula, \"rice\"."
